lane: mail-pop3
why: okay-mail sends and cannot receive, and the consumer who argued
  against bundling receiving (okay-chat) is now blocked by it: their
  service writes one-time codes and match notifications and cannot
  hear the answer. specs/mail.md says receiving "is IMAP or POP, a
  different and much larger module" — true of IMAP, and not of POP3,
  which is eight commands over the socket and TLS this module has.
how: specs/mail.md gains a "Receiving — POP3" section (written first),
  then Pop3.scala beside Smtp.scala: a `Wire` (line, block, write,
  upgrade) with the conversation over it pure and testable against a
  scripted wire, and a socket implementation of that Wire. UIDL for a
  stable identity, RETR up to `most`, and DELE only for what the
  caller's `handle` said it has taken responsibility for — QUIT is
  what commits the deletion, so a session that dies mid-pass deletes
  nothing.
